    <briefdescription>
<para>Resource leak detector for testing. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tracks allocation and deallocation counts to verify that all resources are properly cleaned up.</para>
<para>Example: <programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">ResourceCounter<sp/>counter;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>ptr<sp/>=<sp/>std::make_unique&lt;MyResource&gt;();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>EXPECT_EQ(counter.allocations(),<sp/>1);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>EXPECT_EQ(counter.deallocations(),<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">EXPECT_EQ(counter.allocations(),<sp/>1);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">EXPECT_EQ(counter.deallocations(),<sp/>1);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">EXPECT_EQ(counter.outstanding(),<sp/>0)<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Memory<sp/>leaked!&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
